# Repository engineering workflow

Follow the repository's [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) engineering workflow for every change.

- Define acceptance criteria and a plan before changing production code.
- Write/update automated tests first; for bugs, write a reproducing regression test first.
- For non-trivial work, separate test/spec, implementation, and independent-review ownership.
- Give each delegated feature/fix its own temporary managed Git worktree and `left-try/` branch; never edit the shared checkout concurrently.
- Create one PR per feature/fix, with acceptance criteria, test evidence, execution results, and reviewer comments; keep its worktree only while the PR is active, then safely remove it after merge or formal abandonment.
- Iterate red → minimum green → refactor, running focused tests and the relevant suite at each increment.
- Review tests as rigorously as code: cover relevant boundaries, invalid/missing input, failures, state/order/idempotency/concurrency, security, and integration paths.
- Never weaken or skip tests merely to make the build pass.
- Completion requires an approved feature PR, independent test-and-code review, applicable tests, lint, typecheck, build, and E2E checks, and reported worktree cleanup.
